From: Di Wu <diwux@google.com>
Date: Fri, 1 Aug 2025 04:28:28 +0000
Subject: dev-cpp/abseil-cpp: Disable ICF for symbolize_test

The SymbolizeSplitTextSections test in symbolize_test.cc fails
when building with Identical Code Folding (--icf=all) enabled. The
test expects several small functions with identical bodies to remain
distinct symbols.

With ICF enabled, the linker merges these functions, causing the
symbolizer to return the same name for all of them and failing the
test's assertions.

This change disables ICF for the absl_symbolize_test target by
adding the `-Wl,--icf=none` linker flag. This ensures the functions
are not merged and allows the test to pass.

BUG=b:425266540
TEST=FEATURE=TEST ebuild-brya dev-cpp/abseil-cpp
---
 absl/debugging/CMakeLists.txt | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/absl/debugging/CMakeLists.txt b/absl/debugging/CMakeLists.txt
index 65e2af8..6f49f1d 100644
--- a/absl/debugging/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/absl/debugging/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -111,3 +111,9 @@
     absl::symbolize
     GTest::gmock
 )
+if(ABSL_BUILD_TESTING)
+  if(CMAKE_COMPILER_IS_GNUCXX OR CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "Clang")
+    # The SymbolizeSplitTextSections test requires that ICF is disabled.
+    target_link_options(absl_symbolize_test PRIVATE -Wl,--icf=none)
+  endif()
+endif()
 
 # Internal-only target, do not depend on directly.
 absl_cc_library(
